# Modern Web Guidance (Cursor mirror of rules/02-modern-web-guidance.md)

> Canonical source: `rules/02-modern-web-guidance.md`. If they differ, canonical wins.
> Source: https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src

- Always-on layer: governs HOW you write CSS/JS, regardless of component library.
- Install once: `npx modern-web-guidance@latest install`
- Search BEFORE coding (every task):
  - `npx modern-web-guidance@latest search "<task>"`
  - `npx modern-web-guidance@latest retrieve "<guide-id>"`
  - `npx modern-web-guidance@latest legacy-scan .` (before refactors)
- Prefer native platform APIs (Popover, dialog, Anchor Positioning, View Transitions, container queries, oklch, :user-invalid…) over JS libs/polyfills.
- Lightweight fallbacks only. Accessibility + performance by default (labels, alt, keyboard).
- Cite the guide ID you retrieved in your response.
